{
  "about": [
    "Filters and the samples each shows on a dataset without objects, by contract g7 (one rule everywhere): a row",
    "with no value for a field never matches a comparison of it, nor the NOT of one; an empty list in a field is a",
    "value (changed 2026-11-26), so a negation shows it; and by contract g9: `is null` shows the rows with no value,",
    "so not an empty list (but for tags), and `is empty` the rows whose list holds nothing. By contract g10 a list",
    "field kept in a column of its own (`pests`, made with array-fields; a sample's `array_fields` here, a sample",
    "without one never set) is read as a list in a field is. Run by the server on a database and by the SDK on a",
    "sort_by_similarity result, which asks the server (backend/tests/test_one_rule_filter_cases.py, contract 2.2,",
    "changed 2026-11-25): every case shows the samples named here on both, and none is refused."
  ],
